      "content": "Fever and rash can definitely be symptoms of a viral infection, which are relatively common in young children. However, persistent rash and red spots may also indicate other conditions like infections (like impetigo) or allergic reactions. It would be best to monitor his symptoms, stay hydrated, and consult a pediatrician to rule out any potentially serious conditions. They may also take a sample from the rash area to diagnose correctly.",
